Welcome back. A session that runs too long is where quality quietly dies. Let it bloat and drift,

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
and the model follows your instructions worse while every call costs more. Knowing how to reset

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
is the fix. This lesson covers compacting, clearing, and starting fresh, and when to reach for each.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Let's start with the three moves you have, from lightest to heaviest. First, compact. You summarize

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
the older history into a tight recap, keep your recent turns and key decisions, and free up a big

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
chunk of space, all without losing the thread. Second, clear. You wipe the conversation and

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
start the same session over with an empty window, dropping everything that came before. Third, start

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
fresh. You open a brand new session entirely and re-ground it from your clawed .md and memory,

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
which is the right call when the old session has really drifted. Three levers, and the one you pick

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
depends on how much you want to keep versus how much you want gone. Let's put the two similar

11
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,000
sounding ones side by side, because people mix them up. Compacting preserves continuity.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
It summarizes your older turns down to a recap, but it keeps the thread going, so your recent

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
decisions and the task you're on survive in condensed form. You barely feel the seam. Clearing

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
is the opposite. It empties the window completely in the same session, and nothing from the prior

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
conversation carries forward at all. Reach for clearing when the current context has become more

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
baggage than help, and you genuinely want a blank slate. So the quick test is this. Do you want to

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
keep going with less weight? Compact. Do you want to wipe and restart in place? Clear. Here's the

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
thing to really understand about compaction. It isn't lossless. It's a summary, and summaries

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,000
throw detail away, so you need to know what's protected and what isn't. The good news is your

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:05,000
project root clawed .md is safe. It gets re-read from disk and re-injected after a compaction,

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
so your standing rules survive intact. Recent turns and key decisions are kept in the summary

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,000
too. What can fall away is early prompt detail, the fine points from the start of the conversation,

23
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:25,000
and nested clawed .md files in subdirectories, which don't re-inject on their own. So the lesson

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:32,000
is simple. If a piece of guidance has to survive, put it in your project root config, not in an early

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:38,000
message that a summary might quietly drop. Let's get specific about three things and whether they

26
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:47,000
survive a reset. First, your project root clawed .md. It's re-read from disk and re-injected after

27
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,000
a compaction, so those instructions persist through every reset you do. That's the reliable one.

28
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Second, nested clawed .md files, the ones sitting in subdirectories. These aren't re-injected

29
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:07,000
automatically. They only reload the next time clawed reads a file in that same subdirectory,

30
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,000
so don't count on them mid-session. Third, conversation-only notes. Anything you said in

31
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:20,000
chat but never wrote down simply doesn't survive. If it matters, add it to clawed .md so it's there

32
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:29,000
next time. Root config persists, nested reloads lazily, and unsaved chat is gone. So when is a

33
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:34,000
brand new session the right answer instead of compacting? A few situations call for it. The

34
