bloat, when junk has piled up faster than pruning can keep pace with. And the third is a genuine

37
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,000
task switch, when you're moving to something unrelated that shares no useful context with

38
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
what you were doing. In all three cases, you open a fresh window and re-ground it from your config

39
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,000
and memory. You're not losing anything important, because the durable stuff was never in the window

40
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:14,000
to begin with. Beyond the in-session moves, four settings give you longer-term control over session

41
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:21,000
state. The first is a retention setting, cleanup period days, which controls how long your session

42
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:27,000
data stays on disk before it's cleaned up, defaulting to 30 days. The second is file

43
